`support/Makefile.in` links the build-time `man2html` helper with `CC_FOR_BUILD`
but hands it the *host's* `LIBS`:

    LIBS = @LIBS@
    LIBS_FOR_BUILD = ${LIBS}		# XXX

    man2html$(EXEEXT): $(OBJ1)
    	$(CC_FOR_BUILD) $(LDFLAGS_FOR_BUILD) $(OBJ1) -o $@ ${LIBS_FOR_BUILD}

`configure` already computes the right value -- when cross-compiling it sets
`LIBS_FOR_BUILD=""` (configure.ac, the `cross_compiling` branch) -- and both
the top-level `Makefile.in` and `builtins/Makefile.in` use it.  Only this file
ignores the substitution, and upstream flagged it `XXX` itself.

The result on an illumos cross build, once `libsocket`/`libnsl` are packaged
and `configure` puts them in `LIBS`, is that those target-only libraries reach
a link performed by the *native* toolchain:

    gcc -g man2html.o -o man2html -lsocket -lnsl -ldl
    ld.bfd: cannot find -lsocket: No such file or directory
    ld.bfd: cannot find -lnsl: No such file or directory

Use the substituted value, like the other two makefiles do.

--- support/Makefile.in
+++ support/Makefile.in
@@ -54,7 +54,7 @@
 LOCAL_DEFS = @LOCAL_DEFS@
 
 LIBS = @LIBS@
-LIBS_FOR_BUILD = ${LIBS}		# XXX
+LIBS_FOR_BUILD = @LIBS_FOR_BUILD@
 
 LOCAL_LDFLAGS = @LOCAL_LDFLAGS@
 LDFLAGS = @LDFLAGS@ $(LOCAL_LDFLAGS)
